SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"provisional_id":"RECON-COD-2022-002","canonical_fact_key":"tshisekedi_consolidated_parliamentary_authority_sacred_union","disposition":"accepted","chapter_ids":["1B","4B","7B","8B"],"methodology_ids":["1B.*","4B.*","7B.*","8B.*"],"url":"https://www.everycrsreport.com/files/2022-03-25_R43166_8f90645244ea5367f4d0b0dfdda0952a0b75a8e0.pdf","claim":"A March 2022 Congressional Research Service report states that Tshisekedi broke with Joseph Kabila and assembled a new parliamentary majority in early 2021, materially increasing his governing authority by 2022.","locator":"Opening political background and executive-summary discussion of Tshisekedi's break with Kabila and formation of a new majority coalition","publisher":"Congressional Research Service","publication_date":"2022-03-25","period_fit":"describes the governing arrangement in force entering and during 2022","attribution_limits":"A coalition majority does not prove disciplined control over coalition members, provincial authorities, courts, or security services.","contrary_evidence":"The Sacred Union was heterogeneous and patronage-driven, while entrenched Kabila-era actors and weak institutions remained constraints."}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"provisional_id":"RECON-COD-2022-003","canonical_fact_key":"state_of_siege_repression_2022","disposition":"accepted","chapter_ids":["2B","3B","4B","7B","8B"],"methodology_ids":["2B.*","3B.*","4B.*","7B.*","8B.*"],"url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/03/22/dr-congo-martial-law-brings-crackdown-east","claim":"Under the presidentially initiated state of siege, military and police authorities in North Kivu and Ituri curtailed expression and assembly and arbitrarily detained or prosecuted activists, journalists, and opposition members; security forces killed activist Mumbere Ushindi during a January 2022 protest.","locator":"Lines 616-627, especially 616-621","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-03-22","period_fit":"direct reporting on January-March 2022 and the continuing policy","attribution_limits":"The state-of-siege policy has a presidential nexus, but the source does not show that Tshisekedi ordered each specific abuse.","contrary_evidence":"The administration justified the measure as necessary to combat lethal armed-group insecurity; emergency conditions may explain the policy but do not resolve proportionality or accountability concerns."}

